>
  <p>
    I am a software engineer with 20+ years of experience building software
    across a variety of industries. Early in my career, I was a full-stack
    developer, but as my career progressed, I became more specialized in
    frontend, design systems, developer experience and tooling, and solving
    scale problems, both technical and organizational.
  </p>

  <p>
    I enjoy working at the intersection of developer experience and user
    experience. I have led both UI platform and design system teams, building
    tools and patterns that help developers and designers build better products
    faster.
  </p>

  <p>
    I've led large-scale platform migrations, built developer tooling used
    across a dozen product teams, and grown a design system into the shared
    foundation both designers and engineers build on. The latter has evolved
    into an agentic design system with skills, MCP servers and CLI tooling to
    serve both humans and AI agents.
  </p>

  <p>
    Beyond the systems themselves, I care about how teams work. I've been lucky
    to work with impressive people throughout my career, and helping engineers
    grow through mentorship has been one of the most rewarding parts of the job.
  </p>

  <p>
    As a lifelong learner, the rise of AI makes this an exciting time in
    software engineering. The way we build software is fundamentally changing,
    roles are collapsing and processes are being rewritten. Engineering
    fundamentals and good judgment — technical and product — matter more than
    ever, and I look forward to evolving with this new technology to keep
    building great software.
  </p>
</Layout>
